.Sh DESCRIPTION
The RC2 encryption algorithm for EVP.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_rc2_cbc(), EVP_rc2_cfb(), EVP_rc2_cfb64(), EVP_rc2_ecb(), EVP_rc2_ofb()
RC2 encryption algorithm in CBC, CFB, ECB and OFB modes respectively.
This is a variable key length cipher with an additional parameter called
"effective key bits" or "effective key length".
By default both are set to 128 bits.
.It EVP_rc2_40_cbc(), EVP_rc2_64_cbc()
RC2 algorithm in CBC mode with a default key length and effective key
length of 40 and 64 bits.
.Pp
WARNING: these functions are obsolete.
Their usage should be replaced with the
.Fn EVP_rc2_cbc ,
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_CTX_set_key_length 3
and
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl 3
functions to set the key length and effective key length.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling these functions multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_CIPHER-RC2 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return an
.Sy EVP_CIPHER
structure that contains the implementation of the symmetric cipher.
See
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_CIPHER
structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
